From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:28:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpu: apple,s8003-gpu: Say which interrupt is the
 firmware's

The driver gives the firmware the address of the interrupt controller
and the number of the interrupt it raises towards the host: the last of
the node's five. The other four are not assigned yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,s8003-gpu.yaml     | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,s8003-gpu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,s8003-gpu.yaml
index 9539108..b29f915 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,s8003-gpu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,s8003-gpu.yaml
@@ -30,8 +30,16 @@ properties:
       - const: fender
 
   interrupts:
-    minItems: 5
-    maxItems: 5
+    items:
+      - description: GPU interrupt 0
+      - description: GPU interrupt 1
+      - description: GPU interrupt 2
+      - description: GPU interrupt 3
+      - description:
+          The firmware's interrupt to the host, a software interrupt of the
+          interrupt controller. The firmware raises it through that
+          controller's registers, so the host tells it their address and
+          the interrupt's number.
 
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
